# lambda-call

A lambda bound to a local `val` and invoked directly — the shape real code writes
constantly (`val f = …; f(x)`) and the one **no other corpus row contains**: every
other higher-order workload passes its lambda as an ARGUMENT to a collection method,
which takes a different and much faster runtime path.

Measured 2026-07-30 on the v2 bytecode lane, 100k invocations each, medians of 3 rounds:

| what is called | ns / call |
|---|---|
| closure invoked by `foreach` | 7.1 |
| top-level `def` (`INVOKESTATIC`) | 11.2 |
| **this shape** | **48.7** |

Without this row the defect is invisible to the benchmark and any fix for it is
unprotected against regression. See `TASK/v2-perfomance.md` v2-perf-6b.

```scalascript
def workload(): Long =
  val f = (x: Int) => 0L
  var sum = 0L
  var i = 0
  while i < 100000 do
    sum = sum + f(i)
    i = i + 1
  sum
```
